  "synonym_discrimination": null,
  "usage_note": "This entry covers **yesterday** used as a noun: as the subject of a sentence (*yesterday was cold*), with **'s** (*yesterday's game*), or after a preposition (*since yesterday*). When it says when something happened (*I saw her yesterday*), **yesterday** is an adverb, which has its own entry. For the evening before today, say **last night**, not *yesterday night*.",
